<title>USA: US DAP flat to up, ammonia unchanged, trade quiet.</title>
<headline>US DAP flat to up, ammonia unchanged, trade quiet.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prices for diammonium phosphate were unchanged to higher and ammonia was flat in seasonally quiet trade, cash sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;Its very quiet,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>Ammonia dealers are awaiting the beginning of &quot;side-dress&quot; season in a week to ten days. Side-dressing occurs when farmers apply ammonia to newly emerged corn.</p>
<p>				 Dlrs/short ton   Chg from Friday</p>
<p>DAP central Fla		174-176		 unc</p>
<p>DAP central La Gulf	  188-189		 up 3-1</p>
<p>Ammonia/La Gulf		168-170		 unc</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
